# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audio â€” none of it belongs in the repo
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The clips are excerpts of someone else's film, and the songs are commercial
# recordings. Both are fine to hold locally for a personal project and neither
# should be published. Everything here is also regenerable from sources kept
# outside the repo, so nothing is lost by excluding it.
*.wav
*.mp3
*.mp4
*.m4a
*.flac
*.ogg
*.opus
*.aac
*.wma
*.aiff
*.aif
*.mkv
*.mov
*.webm
*.avi

# Songs in, memes out.
input/
output/

# Cached stems and analysis: large, and rebuilt from the input on demand.
work/

# The word bank and everything feeding it. words.json is only an index of
# audio that is not published either, so it goes too.
words/
words_chaos/

# Local scratch, source material, anything personal.
.local/
scratch/
tmp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
*.egg
build/
dist/
.eggs/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# Tooling caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/
.hypothesis/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Models and heavy downloads
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Whisper weights, Demucs checkpoints and anything else pulled at runtime.
# These are gigabytes and are fetched on demand.
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.onnx
*.safetensors
models/
checkpoints/
.cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# docs/ and src/ and tests/ carry everything needed to rebuild all of the above
# from your own source material. The repo is the tool, not the media.

